// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/compiler/ir/t27_ir_v1.t27 -- t27_ir_v1, the external IR contract.

; This file is a versioned specification. It is not a compiler, not a parser,
; and not a serializer. Nothing in t27b reads this file yet.

; Two systems stay separate. Never put them in one table.
;   A. Target emitters (t27c): t27 -> C / Rust / Zig / Verilog / Python.
;      gen-c, gen-rust, gen-zig, gen-verilog emit source. gen-python is
;      declaration-only (function bodies are not emitted). gen-c is an
;      emitter FROM t27 INTO C. t27b does not participate.
;   B. Shared backend (not built): C / Rust / Zig / Go / Python -> t27 IR
;      -> t27b -> AArch64. t27b lowers t27 IR. It must not parse C, Rust,
;      Go, or Python. Each language needs its own frontend. No such
;      frontend exists in this repository.

; The large goal is a pluggable codegen layer for a language that has
; a frontend lowering to t27 IR. Architecture analogies, not performance
; claims, and not a statement that t27b accepts t27_ir_v1:
; Rust already has pluggable codegen via rustc_codegen_ssa (Cranelift,
; GCC). Go has its own SSA backend. CPython compiles to bytecode and
; interprets it. The niche is a lightweight, verifiable, pluggable
; codegen backend for DSLs, embedded workloads, fast CI, JIT warmup,
; and hardware/software co-design. Not a full production replacement
; of LLVM. First target remains AArch64. Other targets later.
; Cross-language reuse is a goal, not a demonstrated result.
; A shared t27 IR can also support language-to-language lowering,
; including cycles. This is not automatic. Each input language needs a
; frontend, each output language needs an emitter, and each path needs
; a semantic-preservation check. The shape is a star, not a matrix:
;   C      --c2t27-->   t27 IR --gen-rust--> Rust
;   Rust   --rust2t27--> t27 IR --gen-c-->    C
;   Zig    --zig2t27-->  t27 IR --gen-zig-->  Zig
;   Python --py2t27-->   t27 IR --gen-rust--> Rust
; N input languages and M output languages require N+M components, not
; N times M translators. That gain is architecture, not a measurement.
; Outgoing half, partial: gen-c, gen-rust, gen-zig, gen-verilog exist.
; gen-python is declaration-only. Incoming half is missing: c2t27 is
; not written; Rust, Zig, Go, and Python frontends are future work.
; A versioned t27 IR contract is intended to permit restricted
; cross-language lowering among supported language subsets and shared
; use of the t27b AArch64 backend. That is not a present property.
; The proposed star requires a frontend and a target emitter for each
; supported language. It does not imply lossless source-to-source
; translation, preservation of language-specific idioms, or support
; for arbitrary programs.
; Status, not upgraded:
;   gen-c, gen-rust, gen-zig, gen-verilog | t27 -> target | implemented emitters
;   gen-python | t27 -> Python declarations | partial
;   c2t27 | C subset -> t27 IR | planned
;   rust2t27, zig2t27, go2t27, py2t27 | language subset -> t27 IR | future
;   Versioned contract document | t27 IR interchange representation
;     | Specified; t27b does not yet accept or validate this contract
;   shared t27b backend | t27 IR -> AArch64 | current t27 path; external reuse unmeasured
; The versioned t27 IR contract is currently a specification rather
; than a t27b input interface: t27b does not yet accept textual or
; binary t27_ir_v1 representations, verify contract hashes, or run a
; contract validator.
; C -> t27 IR -> C is not required to match the original C byte for byte.
; The requirement, when a path exists, is a semantically equivalent
; program: same observable result, compatible ABI for exported
; functions, and the same declared check policy. Rust ownership, borrow
; checking, traits, macros, and async do not map one-to-one. Zig
; comptime, error unions, and the allocator model need an explicit
; encoding or a restricted subset. Python dynamic typing, objects,
; closures, exceptions, and the runtime library do not lower directly
; without runtime support. C undefined behavior, varargs, complex
; struct layouts, and concurrency stay out of the MVP.
; First measurable milestone, future, not done. The C contour, not Zig:
;   C subset -> c2t27 -> t27_ir_v1 representation -> validator -> t27b
;   -> AArch64 object -> linked binary -> differential test vs clang -O2
; Not a C/Rust/Zig/Python cycle.
; Zig is a future input, not a function. zig2t27 does not exist.
; Zig can be lowered to .t27 only by a separate frontend that parses
; Zig, checks semantics, and lowers a supported subset into the
; versioned t27 IR. .t27 is an intermediate representation, not Zig
; in another syntax. The frontend must preserve types, evaluation
; order, overflow/trap policy, calls, control flow, memory effects,
; and the subset boundary. gen-zig is the outgoing half and exists.
; zig2t27 is the missing incoming half. Today t27 -> Zig is possible.
; An arbitrary .zig file cannot be turned into a correct .t27.
; c2t27, rust2t27, go2t27, and py2t27 are not written. t27b lowers
; the current internal t27 IR to AArch64 only.
; Future zig2t27 acceptance set, not implemented: i32, u32, bool;
; fn, calls, return; if, while, for; local var and const; fixed-size
; arrays; explicit arithmetic with a stated overflow policy; explicit
; casts.
; A future Zig frontend may lower a restricted, explicitly specified
; Zig subset to the versioned t27 IR contract. Constructs outside the
; subset, including comptime evaluation, allocators, error unions,
; optional pointers, slices, closures, async functions, variadic
; functions, and arbitrary foreign-function interfaces, must be
; rejected with explicit diagnostics rather than approximately
; translated.
; Conditional, not current: zig2t27 lowers a defined Zig subset to
; the t27 IR contract, with differential tests of the original Zig
; program, the t27-IR-derived target, and the t27b AArch64 binary.
; Promises: restricted Zig to t27 IR only after zig2t27; t27 IR to
; Zig source yes because gen-zig exists; Zig to AArch64 via t27b only
; after contract validation and the backend path; any Zig file no;
; same Zig source text not required; Rust without losing idioms no;
; any language to any language no.
; A Zig round trip may be semantically equivalent and textually
; different. Names, comments, formatting, comptime structure, and
; idioms are not reconstructed.
; First Zig experiment, future, not this milestone:
;   Zig subset -> zig2t27 -> t27 IR -> gen-c -> clang -> binary -> run
;   Zig subset -> zig2t27 -> t27 IR -> t27b -> AArch64 -> binary -> run
; Compare output hashes, exit codes, traps or panics, and observable
; side effects. gen-rust as a third target and reverse rust2t27 come
; after that.
; Artifact checklist:
;   t27_ir_v1.t27 human-readable contract: present as a document
;   canonical textual IR: not implemented
;   binary IR: not implemented
;   IR hash: not implemented
;   validator: not implemented
;   t27b reader: not implemented
;   differential harness: not implemented
; The sentence "t27b is a shared backend for t27 and a defined C
; subset" stays conditional until all of the following exist: one
; fixed C subset; a versioned t27 IR contract; c2t27; identical inputs
; and expected output hashes; separate c2t27, t27b-backend, and
; end-to-end compile times; object size, runtime, and dynamic-instruction
; counts; an explicit runtime-check policy. None of that evidence is
; recorded here.
; Smallest closed contour, future, not done:
;   C subset -> c2t27 -> t27 IR -> gen-rust -> rustc -> binary -> run
;   paired with C subset -> clang -O2 -> binary -> run
; Reverse only after that subset is supported, also not done:
;   Rust subset -> rust2t27 -> t27 IR -> gen-c -> clang -> binary -> run
; Emitter time is separate from t27b backend time on a source-to-source
; path. It is not folded into t27b build. Every cell is not measured.
; A full circular translation is not claimed. It would require at least
; two frontends, a versioned IR contract, and differential tests in
; both directions. None of those exist now.

; Layer map (goal, not a result):
;   Frontend   Clang, rustc frontend, Zig, Go, CPython | c2t27 rust2t27 zig2t27 go2t27 py2t27
;   IR         LLVM IR | t27 IR
;   Middle-end LLVM optimizations | t27 optimizer (not part of this study)
;   Backend    LLVM AArch64 / Cranelift / GCC | t27b AArch64
;   Target     x86-64, AArch64, RISC-V, WASM | AArch64 first, then others

; An internal IR already exists, and it is not this contract.
; Observed on master checkout /Users/playra/t27-build at commit be7934fe53,
; file cli/t27b/src/ir.rs (this lane, lane/t27-lagger-spec, does not contain
; that file). That IR is a typed in-memory tree (Program, Func, Stmt, Expr)
; produced by lower from the t27 AST and consumed by the interpreter and the
; AArch64 codegen. It has no version field, no textual form, no general
; binary container, no content hash, and no validator of an external file.
; A wasm32 fact-table projection (wasm_facts) is a target table, not this
; contract's binary form. There is no IR text dump.

; Status codes used below:
;   0 ABSENT          -- not in the internal tree and not an external artifact
;   1 INTERNAL_ONLY   -- present in cli/t27b/src/ir.rs, not an external contract
;   2 EXTERNAL        -- a versioned artifact t27b actually consumes
; No row in this file is 2. A test locks that.

; ASCII only (L3). English only. phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module T27IrV1;

use t27os::session_store::put_bytes;
use t27os::session_store::put_dec;
use t27os::editors::same_bytes;
use fpga::sha256::sha256_one_block;
use fpga::sha256::iv;

pub const CONTRACT_NAME : str = "t27_ir_v1";
pub const CONTRACT_VERSION : u8 = 1;

pub const STATUS_ABSENT : u8 = 0;
pub const STATUS_INTERNAL_ONLY : u8 = 1;
pub const STATUS_EXTERNAL : u8 = 2;

; --- Required properties of the external contract ---------------------
; Textual form, binary form, content hash, validator, and deterministic
; serialization are required and are not yet implemented.
pub const FORM_TEXT : u8 = 0;
pub const FORM_BINARY : u8 = 0;
pub const FORM_HASH : u8 = 0;
pub const FORM_VALIDATOR : u8 = 0;
pub const FORM_DETERMINISTIC_SERIALIZATION : u8 = 0;
; The normative UB and ABI paragraphs in this file are the contract text.
; t27b does not load them. The internal tree has related fields (see below).
pub const FORM_UB_POLICY_ARTIFACT : u8 = 0;
pub const FORM_ABI_CONTRACT_ARTIFACT : u8 = 0;
pub const FORM_TARGET_INDEPENDENT_METADATA : u8 = 0;

; --- Schema outline (required contents). Status is the internal tree. --
; module, functions
pub const HAS_MODULE : u8 = 1; // Program.module
pub const HAS_FUNCTIONS : u8 = 1; // Program.funcs / Func
; types named by this contract
pub const HAS_I8 : u8 = 1;
pub const HAS_I16 : u8 = 1;
pub const HAS_I32 : u8 = 1;
pub const HAS_I64 : u8 = 1;
pub const HAS_U8 : u8 = 1;
pub const HAS_U16 : u8 = 1;
pub const HAS_U32 : u8 = 1;
pub const HAS_U64 : u8 = 1;
pub const HAS_BOOL : u8 = 1;
pub const HAS_F32 : u8 = 1;
pub const HAS_F64 : u8 = 1;
; constants, arithmetic, comparisons
pub const HAS_CONSTANTS : u8 = 1; // ExprKind::Const
pub const HAS_ARITH : u8 = 1; // ArithOp
pub const HAS_CMP : u8 = 1; // CmpOp
; control flow. The internal IR is a statement tree (If, While, Break,
; Continue, Return, Select). It is not a basic-block CFG.
pub const HAS_STRUCTURED_IF : u8 = 1;
pub const HAS_STRUCTURED_WHILE : u8 = 1;
pub const HAS_BASIC_BLOCKS : u8 = 0; // not yet implemented
pub const HAS_EXPLICIT_BRANCHES : u8 = 0; // not yet implemented
; memory. Slots are fixed-size frame objects. Ty has Ptr. There is no
; first-class array type in Ty; fixed arrays are not a contract type yet.
pub const HAS_LOCALS : u8 = 1; // Func.vars
pub const HAS_FIXED_ARRAY_TYPE : u8 = 0; // not yet implemented as a Ty
pub const HAS_POINTERS : u8 = 1; // Ty::Ptr, Load, Store, Offset
pub const HAS_CALLS : u8 = 1; // ExprKind::Call
; overflow. Internal OverflowMode is Trap (language default) or Wrap.
pub const HAS_OVERFLOW_MODE : u8 = 1;

; Internal types that this contract does not include. Recording them stops
; a later edit from silently treating them as part of t27_ir_v1.
pub const INTERNAL_HAS_PTR : u8 = 1;
pub const INTERNAL_HAS_I128 : u8 = 1;
pub const INTERNAL_HAS_ODD_WIDTHS : u8 = 1; // Ty::UN / Ty::IN
pub const CONTRACT_INCLUDES_I128 : u8 = 0;
pub const CONTRACT_INCLUDES_ODD_WIDTHS : u8 = 0;

; --- Undefined-behaviour policy (normative for t27_ir_v1) -------------
; Integer + - * on the contract integer types trap on overflow in the
; default mode. A wrap mode exists internally for differential testing
; (ArithOp AddW/SubW/MulW and OverflowMode::Wrap). Division by zero traps.
; A checked shift traps when the amount is outside 0..bitwidth; a wrapping
; shift reduces the amount modulo the width. These are defined trap or
; wrap behaviours inside the internal IR, not C signed-overflow UB.
; Provenance, uninitialised reads, data races, and an out-of-object load
; or store are not given a value. The first C subset rejects them by name.
; UB_POINTER_PROVENANCE_SPECIFIED, UB_UNINIT_SPECIFIED, and
; UB_RACES_SPECIFIED stay 0: rejection is not a defined semantics.
pub const UB_DEFAULT_IS_TRAP : u8 = 1;
pub const UB_POINTER_PROVENANCE_SPECIFIED : u8 = 0;
pub const UB_UNINIT_SPECIFIED : u8 = 0;
pub const UB_RACES_SPECIFIED : u8 = 0;

; --- ABI contract ------------------------------------------------------
; Observed internal behaviour (cli/t27b/src/ir.rs Program::arg_regs and
; internal_abi), not an external document t27b loads:
;   scalar integers and bool: AAPCS64 integer class, x0-x7;
;   f32/f64: s0-s7 / d0-d7;
;   a function that would pass an argument on the stack, or that passes
;   or returns an aggregate, uses t27b's own convention and is not exported.
; The external ABI contract a foreign frontend could target is not implemented.
pub const ABI_INTERNAL_AAPCS64_SCALARS : u8 = 1;
pub const ABI_EXTERNAL_DOCUMENT : u8 = 0;

; --- Target-independent metadata (required, absent) --------------------
; A future container must carry: contract name, contract version, source
; language identifier, source content hash, overflow mode, and the declared
; runtime-check policy. None of these fields exist on Program.
pub const META_SOURCE_LANGUAGE : u8 = 0;
pub const META_SOURCE_HASH : u8 = 0;
pub const META_CHECK_POLICY : u8 = 0;

; --- Current formula. Do not strengthen. --------------------------------
; "t27 IR" here means the internal IR t27b already lowers, not a claim
; that the external t27_ir_v1 contract is implemented or that foreign
; frontends exist.
pub const CLAIM_CURRENT : str = "t27b is the backend for the t27 IR. It lowers the current t27 IR to AArch64 and serves as the native, JIT, assembly, and Verilog backend for the t27 language. In this sentence, t27 IR denotes the internal representation already lowered by t27b, not the external t27_ir_v1 contract. t27c provides target emitters from t27 to C, Rust, Zig, Verilog, and a declaration-only Python target; it does not provide a t27b backend. Future language frontends may lower restricted C, Rust, Zig, Go, and Python subsets to a versioned t27 IR contract, potentially enabling cross-language lowering and shared use of the t27b AArch64 backend. Cross-language translation and shared-backend reuse are architectural goals, not demonstrated results.";
pub const CLAIM_RESTRICTED_LOWERING : str = "A versioned t27 IR contract is intended to permit restricted cross-language lowering among supported language subsets and shared use of the t27b AArch64 backend.";
pub const STAR_LIMIT : str = "The proposed star requires a frontend and a target emitter for each supported language. It does not imply lossless source-to-source translation, preservation of language-specific idioms, or support for arbitrary programs.";
pub const RESTRICTED_LOWERING_IS_A_RESULT : u8 = 0;
pub const CIRCULAR_TRANSLATION_CLAIMED : u8 = 0;
pub const ANY_LANGUAGE_TO_ANY_LANGUAGE : u8 = 0;
pub const TEXTUAL_ROUND_TRIP_REQUIRED : u8 = 0;
pub const GEN_C_EXISTS : u8 = 1;
